{"title":"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisors</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6792dbe39fce8fb36104857e86e32d26b199d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,240,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_cube\" title=\"Perfect cube\">perfect cubes</a>?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf5bb67c55ab16fbd2b8ba96955e7121d03c6977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3240000=2^7\\cdot 3^4\\cdot 5^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"162\" height=\"15\" />. We want to know how many numbers are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23b10c7af073178266261104ab59f6defb9546e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3a}3^{3b}5^{3c}$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> which divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6792dbe39fce8fb36104857e86e32d26b199d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,240,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />.  This imposes the restrictions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b028b21f4795bdec3d5a4608b46bdf5d3774883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq a\\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea74fdfeb5475305cc42e33709402bfef7039a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq b\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09cbc8e483a28ea25bf6b193f47d4aced22584af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq c\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, which lead to 12 solutions and thus 12 such divisors.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST\">2005 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1